# Click — Board Game Meetup Schedule Voting App

This project is a schedule-voting web app for board game meetups.

## Stack

- Next.js App Router + TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind CSS
- Supabase (`@supabase/ssr`, `@supabase/supabase-js`)
- lucide-react, clsx, tailwind-merge

## TypeScript

- Prefer `type` over `interface` unless declaration merging is needed.
- Do not use `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow.
- Colocate types next to the feature that owns them.
- Import with the `@/` alias (`@/lib/supabase/server`).

## Next.js App Router

- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only for event handlers, browser APIs, or client-only libraries.
- Keep data fetching in Server Components or Server Actions. Do not fetch from the client when the server can do it.
- Put Server Actions in dedicated files or at the bottom of a server module. Mark them with `"use server"`.
- Route files live under `app/`. Shared UI lives under `components/`. Shared helpers live under `lib/`.
- Do not import `lib/supabase/server.ts` into Client Components.
- Do not import `lib/supabase/client.ts` into Server Components, Route Handlers, or Server Actions.

## Supabase SSR

- Browser / Client Components: `import { createClient } from "@/lib/supabase/client"` then `createClient()`.
- Server Components, Server Actions, Route Handlers: `import { createClient } from "@/lib/supabase/server"` then `await createClient()`.
- Always create a new client per request on the server. Do not cache the server client as a module singleton.
- Use the anon/publishable key from `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_*` env vars. Never put the service role key in client code or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Cookie writes from Server Components may no-op; session refresh belongs in middleware when auth is added.

## Tailwind CSS

- Style with Tailwind utility classes. Avoid new CSS modules unless a third-party widget requires them.
- Merge conditional class names with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- Icons come from `lucide-react`.

## UI and product

- Korean UI copy unless a file already uses English.
- Keep layouts readable on mobile first; meetup voting happens on phones.
- Prefer small, focused components over large page files.

## Examples

```ts
// ✅ Client Component
"use client";
import { createClient } from "@/lib/supabase/client";
const supabase = createClient();

// ✅ Server Component / Server Action
import { createClient } from "@/lib/supabase/server";
const supabase = await createClient();

// ❌ Do not create a global supabase singleton for the server
export const supabase = createClient();
```
